{#
   Infrastructure / "Brick by brick" (#facilities). Reworked: the four sector
   cards used to be phone screenshots of each sector screen, and are now a
   full-site isometric hero plus a tile for every facility in that sector, drawn
   by the same engine the game runs on.

   The tiles are NOT listed here. Twig supplies the sector shell — its name,
   colour and blurb, which are copy — and landing.js fills the hero and one tile
   per facility from window.FACILITY_SITES, the sprite bundle's own export of
   which facilities each site has and which game slug each draws as. Hand-listing
   22 facility names in this template would be a second copy of a mapping that is
   generated precisely so there is only one (see FacilitySpriteMap's docblock for
   the PHP half of the same argument).

   These are DECORATIVE: the configs are seeded random, not a real club's
   facilities. The featured club's actual build-out is in the Club Spotlight's own
   Facilities panel, above. That panel reads ClubSpotlight.facilities and shows
   level badges; this section shows what the catalogue contains.

   The upgrade-path row is the one place a single facility is drawn five times at
   five levels. Physio Clinic is the design's choice and a good one — it is the
   first facility most clubs invest in.
#}
<section class="facilities-section" id="facilities" aria-labelledby="facilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-label">Infrastructure</div>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="facilities-title">BRICK BY BRICK</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">Build an isometric empire across four sectors and 22 upgradable facilities, drawn in the same isometric engine the game runs on. Every one governs recovery, development pace, scouting yield or matchday revenue, and every build risks delay.</p>

        <div class="sector-grid">
            <article class="sector-card" data-facility-site="training" aria-labelledby="sector-training-title">
                <header class="sector-head">
                    <h3 class="sector-name pixel is-cyan" id="sector-training-title">TRAINING</h3>
                    <p class="sector-blurb">Accelerates player growth, supports tactical mastery and reduces developmental stalls.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="sector-hero" data-facility-hero>
                    <img alt="Isometric training ground with pitch, gym, technical zone and tactics room" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <ul class="sector-tiles" data-facility-tiles></ul>
            </article>

            <article class="sector-card" data-facility-site="medical" aria-labelledby="sector-medical-title">
                <header class="sector-head">
                    <h3 class="sector-name pixel is-red" id="sector-medical-title">MEDICAL</h3>
                    <p class="sector-blurb">Speeds up rehabilitation, boosts stamina and limits long-term wear.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="sector-hero" data-facility-hero>
                    <img alt="Isometric medical centre with six clinics" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <ul class="sector-tiles" data-facility-tiles></ul>
            </article>

            <article class="sector-card" data-facility-site="scouting" aria-labelledby="sector-scouting-title">
                <header class="sector-head">
                    <h3 class="sector-name pixel is-gold" id="sector-scouting-title">SCOUTING</h3>
                    <p class="sector-blurb">Enlarges youth intake, broadens scouting range and surfaces higher-potential prospects.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="sector-hero" data-facility-hero>
                    <img alt="Isometric scouting complex with HQ, data hub, trial pitch, fleet and academy" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <ul class="sector-tiles" data-facility-tiles></ul>
            </article>

            <article class="sector-card" data-facility-site="stadium" aria-labelledby="sector-stadium-title">
                <header class="sector-head">
                    <h3 class="sector-name pixel is-mint" id="sector-stadium-title">STADIUM</h3>
                    <p class="sector-blurb">Expands capacity, scales commercial revenue and elevates reputation.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="sector-hero" data-facility-hero>
                    <img alt="Isometric stadium with stands, floodlights, scoreboard, shop and car park" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <ul class="sector-tiles" data-facility-tiles></ul>
            </article>
        </div>

        <div class="upgrade-path">
            <h3 class="sector-name pixel is-gold">UPGRADE PATH: PHYSIO CLINIC</h3>
            <p class="section-sub">Every facility grows through five levels. Invest early, then keep up the upkeep: neglect one and players complain, your Facility Manager's morale slides and the club's reputation takes the hit.</p>
            <ol class="upgrade-levels" data-upgrade-path="physio"></ol>
        </div>

        <div class="facility-notes">
            <div class="facility-note">
                <span class="facility-note-title pixel is-mint">Youth Academy intake</span>
                <p>A new intake of prospects arrives at the start of every season. They develop inside the Academy until they turn 16 and become eligible for a first-team contract — the size and quality of each intake scales with your Academy's level.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="facility-note">
                <span class="facility-note-title pixel is-red">Upkeep isn't optional</span>
                <p>Facilities decay over time. Neglect one and players start complaining, your Facility Manager's morale slides toward resignation, and the club's reputation takes the hit — proactive maintenance costs more per week, but it's cheaper than the alternative.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
